805	829	Life cycle, Childhood	Sexual Nonrestraint in Adolescent Boys	Ordinal	The absence of sexual restraints such as taboos or restrictions on heterosexual intercourse and other erotic behavior, including heterosexual play, masturbation, and homosexuality. A high degree of modesty, such as the requirement to keep the genitals constantly covered in public, indicates moderate restraint. Incest taboos, if highly emphasized or widely extended, are considered as indicators of restraint. Note: Sexual nonrestraint = Sexual expression + 1 more or less. The authors indicate the advisability of using the sum of the two scores as a Sexual Freedom index.	Barry, H., & Schlegel, A. (1984). Measurements of adolescent sexual behavior in the standard sample of societies. Ethnology, 23(4), 315-329.	barry1984measurements
