870	917	Economy, Labour, Politics	Historical Frame for Pinpointing Date Where Slaveholding Present	Ordinal	Patterson defines slaveholding as permanent dominant violation of natally alienated and generally dishonored persons. This excludes non-hereditary slavery, and thus does not include what Murdock (1967: 166) classifies as incipient slavery. His focus is on slaveholding societies, and excludes societies largely composed of former slaves.	Patterson, O. (1982). Slavery and social death. Harvard University Press.	patterson1982slavery
